# The contract this portal is generated against.
#
# The OPERATOR contract, not the traveller one. Different document, different
# base path, different auth, and a tenant boundary the traveller API does not
# have: `operator_id` is read from the session row and is never accepted as a
# parameter in any position.
#
# The intent is that both frontends pin one yuvoy-api commit, so they cannot be
# reasoning about different versions of the same backend. They agree today:
# `yuvoy-app` is on this same ref. The two documents are separate files, so a
# change to one says nothing about the other — this bump touches only the
# operator document, and yuvoy-app's bump to the same ref touched only the
# traveller one.
#
# `pnpm contract:check` fails the build if this copy stops matching the ref.
repo=yuvoy-in/yuvoy-api
path=contracts/operator-openapi.yaml
# 10 Sep 2026, tenth bump. Forward from 3a643cde69c0. Four new operations and
# one new schema; nothing was removed and nothing this portal reads changed
# shape.
#
# Consumed in this change:
#   - `GET /commission-owed` (op#40 §2). What the operator owes us on cash we
#     never handled. There is no payout to take it out of, so it is a balance —
#     and the trips behind it are listed, which is the point of the screen.
#
# NOT consumed here, and each needs its own change:
#   - `POST /bookings/{id}/cash-collected` (op#40 §1). The endpoint is fine;
#     the MANIFEST is what is missing. A party carries no fare, no way to tell
#     a cash booking from a card one, and nowhere to read back a collection
#     that was already recorded — so the button cannot be put on the right
#     rows, cannot name an amount, and would forget itself on reload. Raised on
#     yuvoy-operator#40 and reassigned; the screen lands the day the manifest
#     says which parties owe cash.
#   - `POST /experiences/{id}/relist` and `RevisionOutcome`. A listing withdrawn
#     by its operator can be put back on sale; this portal has the withdraw
#     half only. Its own issue.
#   - `POST /slots/{id}/time`. Moving a departure's time. Nothing in the
#     calendar offers it yet.
#   - `202` on the logo upload, for an account already LIVE — a new mark is
#     reviewed before it replaces the one on every reel. The logo screen
#     treats every 2xx alike today and would tell an operator the change is
#     live when it is pending. Its own issue.
#
# `git ls-remote` was the check for this ref, not `gh api .../commits/master`,
# which served a five-minute-stale SHA twice on 8 Sep and cost a retracted
# issue.
